  "problem": "Solve $3(7-4x)^{2}+5<-25.$",
  "worked_solution": "Isolating the quadratic term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(7-4x)^{2}+5 & <-25 \\\\ 3(7-4x)^{2} & <-30 \\\\ (7-4x)^{2} & <-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $(7-4x)^{2}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(2)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to the given inequality.",
